IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cla2-common`
IMPORT `cla2-abuse`

-- Civil Liability Act 2002 (WA) -- baseline-2026-11: cases for Part 2A (cla2-abuse.l4).
-- Every exported question, with edges: each condition of ss 15B and 15D failing in turn, each continuity route of ss 15F
-- and 15G, the 1 July 2018 boundary of ss 15C(7) and 15E(5), the 50% rule of s 15K(4), a deduction equal to and just under
-- the damages, a fee one dollar over the costs determination. Expected values are worked by hand from the deposited text.
-- The facts are illustrative; no real person, institution or firm is meant.
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice.

§ `Cases -- Part 2A`

§§ `Short names for the cases`

`same` MEANS `it is the same institution`
`members and purposes` MEANS `its class of members and its primary purposes or work are substantially the same (s 15F(2))`
`court finds` MEANS `the court finds it substantially the same on other grounds (s 15F(1))`
`merged into` MEANS `none is the same: some or all of the earlier institution merged into it (s 15G(3)(a))`
`merged with others` MEANS `none is the same: some or all of the earlier institution merged with others to form it (s 15G(3)(b))`
`remainder` MEANS `none is the same: it is what remains after part of the earlier institution left (s 15G(3)(c))`
`chain` MEANS `none is the same: it descends through a chain of mergers, remainders or substantially-the-same links (s 15G(2)(b), (4))`
`named by regulation` MEANS `none is the same: a regulation names it as the relevant successor (s 15G(5))`
`gone` MEANS `no institution now is the same, substantially the same or a successor`

`office holder` MEANS `the current holder of the office, in the name of the office (s 15B)`
`head` MEANS `the current head of the institution, as the current office holder (ss 15B, 15H(2))`
`institution` MEANS `the institution itself, which is now incorporated (s 15D)`
`not needed` MEANS `Part 2A is not needed: the office holder still holds the office, and is sued as the general law allows`
`no one` MEANS `Part 2A gives no one to sue on these facts`

-- Arguments, in order: abused; cause of action against the office holder; the Crown; care over children then; incorporated
-- then; incorporated now; how it relates now; a regulation names another successor; office substantially the same now;
-- office holder still holds it; could sue if they still held it.
`sue` MEANS `Whom can I sue for abuse in an institution that was unincorporated`

§§ `ss 15B, 15D, 15F-15H -- whom I can sue`

-- The plain s 15B case: an unincorporated religious body then and now, the same body, the same office, the office holder of
-- the time gone.
#ASSERT `sue` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `same` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `office holder`
-- s 15H(2): no office now the same, but the institution continues: its current head.
#ASSERT `sue` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `same` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `head`
-- s 15D: the institution has since incorporated (s 15F(3)(c): still substantially the same).
#ASSERT `sue` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE `members and purposes` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `institution`
-- s 15D has no "no longer holds the office" condition: the institution even if the office holder is still there.
#ASSERT `sue` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE `same` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `institution`
-- s 15B(1)(e) fails: the office holder still holds the office, so Part 2A is not needed.
#ASSERT `sue` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `same` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `not needed`
-- s 15A: the Crown is not an "institution".
#ASSERT `sue` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE `same` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no one`
-- s 15B(1)(c)(ii): incorporated at the time of the abuse: sue it under the general law, not Part 2A.
#ASSERT `sue` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE `same` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no one`
#ASSERT `sue` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE `same` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no one`
-- s 15B(1)(c)(i): no care, supervision or authority over children at the time.
#ASSERT `sue` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `same` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no one`
-- s 15B(1)(a), (b).
#ASSERT `sue` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `same` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no one`
#ASSERT `sue` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `same` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no one`
-- s 15B(1)(f), s 15D(1)(e): the action could not be maintained even against the office holder of the time.
#ASSERT `sue` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `same` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no one`
#ASSERT `sue` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE `same` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no one`
-- No continuity at all.
#ASSERT `sue` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `gone` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no one`
#ASSERT `sue` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE `gone` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no one`
-- s 15F(1): the court finds it substantially the same.
#ASSERT `sue` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `court finds` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `office holder`
-- s 15G(3)(a): merged into a body that is still unincorporated; no office the same: its head (s 15H(2), (4)(b)).
#ASSERT `sue` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `merged into` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `head`
-- s 15G(7)(a): a regulation naming another successor prevails.
#ASSERT `sue` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `merged into` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no one`
-- s 15G(3)(b): merged with others into an incorporated body.
#ASSERT `sue` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE `merged with others` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `institution`
-- s 15G(3)(c): the remainder.
#ASSERT `sue` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `remainder` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `office holder`
-- s 15G(2)(b), (4): a chain of links.
#ASSERT `sue` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE `chain` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `institution`
-- s 15G(5): named by regulation.
#ASSERT `sue` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `named by regulation` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `office holder`
#ASSERT `sue` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `named by regulation` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `office holder`

§§ `ss 15C, 15E -- what a judgment or settlement can be paid from`

`the office holder liable` MEANS `the holder of an office of authority in the institution, on a cause of action of the s 15B(1)(b) type`

#ASSERT `Can my judgment or settlement be paid from the institution's assets and trusts` `the office holder liable` (Date 1 7 2018) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can my judgment or settlement be paid from the institution's assets and trusts` `the office holder liable` (Date 30 6 2018) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Can my judgment or settlement be paid from the institution's assets and trusts` `an institution` (Date 15 3 2021) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can my judgment or settlement be paid from the institution's assets and trusts` `an institution` (Date 30 6 2018) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Can my judgment or settlement be paid from the institution's assets and trusts` `someone else` (Date 15 3 2021) EQUALS NOTHING

#ASSERT `Can the office holder's personal assets be used to pay me` `the office holder liable` (Date 15 3 2021) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can the office holder's personal assets be used to pay me` `the office holder liable` (Date 1 7 2018) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can the office holder's personal assets be used to pay me` `the office holder liable` (Date 30 6 2018) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Can the office holder's personal assets be used to pay me` `an institution` (Date 15 3 2021) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Can the office holder's personal assets be used to pay me` `someone else` (Date 15 3 2021) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 15K -- earlier redress payments`

-- Arguments: paid for child sexual abuse of me; paid under a judgment or settlement of an earlier action; the payment;
-- the court is satisfied what share was for this abuse; that share.
`deduction` MEANS `How much of an earlier payment is deducted from my damages`
`award` MEANS `How much will I be awarded after the deduction`

-- A redress scheme payment of $150 000, $100 000 of it found to be for the abuse sued on (s 15K(2), (3)).
#ASSERT `deduction` TRUE FALSE 150000 TRUE 100000 EQUALS JUST 100000
-- The court not satisfied of the share: 50% (s 15K(4)).
#ASSERT `deduction` TRUE FALSE 150000 FALSE 0 EQUALS JUST 75000
-- Found to be wholly for other abuse: nothing.
#ASSERT `deduction` TRUE FALSE 150000 TRUE 0 EQUALS JUST 0
-- Not a payment for child sexual abuse (s 15K(1)(a)): nothing.
#ASSERT `deduction` FALSE FALSE 40000 TRUE 40000 EQUALS JUST 0
-- A judgment or settlement of an earlier action (s 15K(1)(b), (5)): s 15K sets no deduction.
#ASSERT `deduction` TRUE TRUE 200000 TRUE 200000 EQUALS NOTHING

-- Damages of $500 000 less 50% of $150 000.
#ASSERT `award` 500000 TRUE FALSE 150000 FALSE 0 EQUALS JUST 425000
-- The deduction exceeds the damages: nothing awarded (fork F5).
#ASSERT `award` 60000 TRUE FALSE 150000 FALSE 0 EQUALS JUST 0
-- Equal to the damages; one dollar under.
#ASSERT `award` 75000 TRUE FALSE 150000 FALSE 0 EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `award` 75001 TRUE FALSE 150000 FALSE 0 EQUALS JUST 1
#ASSERT `award` 500000 FALSE FALSE 40000 TRUE 40000 EQUALS JUST 500000
#ASSERT `award` 500000 TRUE TRUE 200000 TRUE 200000 EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 15L -- the cap on lawyers' fees`

-- Arguments: a costs determination is in force; the most it allows; the reward the agreement gives.
#ASSERT `Is my fee agreement void` TRUE 50000 50001 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my fee agreement void` TRUE 50000 50000 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is my fee agreement void` TRUE 50000 20000 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is my fee agreement void` FALSE 50000 1000000 EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- Void: everything paid for services from 1 July 2018 comes back, not just the excess (s 15L(3), (4)).
#ASSERT `How much of my legal fees can I get back` TRUE 50000 80000 30000 EQUALS JUST 30000
#ASSERT `How much of my legal fees can I get back` TRUE 50000 50000 30000 EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `How much of my legal fees can I get back` FALSE 50000 80000 30000 EQUALS JUST 0
